**Scope.** The eleven Codex commits `eae21dc, 095c2d1, cebfe75, 045ec94, 0640bf2, 47d7c97, 5acae13, ace9383, 21df764, 2e9f64c, b42b559` (the Planner's `a367d06` between the second and third ignored). Files: `tools/exp04_profiles.py` (88 lines), `tools/paired_compare.py` (594), `tests/test_exp04_profiles.py` (146), `tests/test_paired_compare.py` (551). Specification: `coder_prompts/round4_prompt.md`; normative analytic text plan §3, §4 "canonical input selection", §5 rows, §11 A1–A9. Context read before judging: `worklog/experiment_SOP.md`, the plan v4, the notebook entries from 18:11 onward, the round-4 Coder transcript's final report, `tools/paired_stats.py` (`_bootstrap_ratios`, `diff_in_diff_bootstrap`, `equivalence_tost`, `bonferroni_alpha`), `tools/summarize_yaw.py` conventions, `tools/provenance.py`, `tools/exp04_eval.py` and `tools/exp04_eval_launch.py` at `b42b559`.

**Method.** All reading and execution on an isolated clone of the repository checked out at `b42b559` (`<scratchpad>/r4/r4_clone`, with `ckpt/yaw_aug/reference_manifest*.json`, `reference_manifests_index.json` and the two epoch-12 checkpoints symlinked in) — the Coder's round-3b fix was writing to the real working tree concurrently. No tracked file of the real repository was modified; this review file is the only file created there. Every §3 rule was re-derived independently (own quantile definition, own resample-index generator replicating `paired_stats`' chunked RNG, hand-built masks, synthetic five-seed data with known shifts), and admission was attacked with 31 additional mutations beyond the Coder's 13.

## Summary verdict

**Approve with changes** (no blocking findings). The statistics implement plan §3 exactly; admission is fail-closed against every mutation I tried and writes nothing on refusal; the profiles are literal, immutable and every pinned identity reproduces from the files on disk; commit hygiene is clean. The changes below are for the A9 refactor commit and for round 5's reuse — none affects the correctness of what was delivered in this round.

## Findings

### Should-fix

**1. `tools/paired_compare.py:307-309` — the `launcher` approved pin is checked against the *evaluation-launcher* (writer) closure, so `launcher` and `writer` are forced equal.**
